# Tutorial 08 — the 3D view: orbiting, visual styles, materials and textures, the section box.
title: 3D and materials
summary: The 3D view, orbiting, visual styles, materials and textures, and the section box
---
open sample "Cedar House"
caption "The 3D view" "The model is always live: every plan edit shows in 3D"
click mode 3D
wait 1.5
camera Aerial
wait 1.5
caption "Orbit" "Drag to orbit, scroll to zoom, the view cube jumps to standard views"
orbit 90 5
wait 1
caption "Visual styles" "VSCURRENT: Realistic, Shaded, Hidden line, Conceptual, X-ray, Sketchy"
style Realistic
wait 2
style Hidden
wait 2
style Conceptual
wait 2
style Sketchy
wait 2
style Realistic
camera Corner
wait 1.5
caption "Materials" "Colour, roughness, metalness, transparency and textures"
click panel Materials
wait 3.5
caption "Assign a material" "Pick in the plan, then CHPROP Material"
click mode Split
wait 1.5
pick 8500,0
type CHPROP Material Limestone ;
wait 2.5
note "The cedar tower wall is now limestone" top for 3
wait 2.5
type U
escape
wait 1.5
caption "Section box" "Cut the model live to look inside"
click mode 3D
type SECTIONBOX Level
wait 2
orbit -40 4
wait 1.5
type SECTIONBOX Off
wait 1
click panel Properties
caption "Next: rendering" "Tutorial 09 renders the house"
wait 3
